# Project Christina: FastMCP JSON-RPC 2.0 API Reference

> **Complete Protocol Specification, Schemas & Tool Reference** for Project Christina FastMCP Gateway (`christina.bridge.mcp_server`).

---

## 1. FastMCP Gateway Overview

The **Christina FastMCP Gateway** implements the [Model Context Protocol (MCP)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) specification over standard input/output streams (`stdio`) using pure Python standard library JSON-RPC 2.0 framing.

### Starting the Server
```bash
python3 -m christina.bridge.mcp_server
```

### Protocol Lifecycle
1. **Initialization (`initialize`)**: Handshake establishing client-server capability negotiation.
2. **Tool Discovery (`tools/list`)**: Returns schemas for the 4 canonical MCP tools.
3. **Tool Invocation (`tools/call`)**: Executes a specific tool with arguments and returns structured output.
4. **Lifecycle Hooks**: In-process hooks for Google Antigravity CLI (`agy`) and OpenCode.

---

## 2. Standard JSON-RPC 2.0 Framing

All messages exchanged over stdio are single-line JSON strings terminated by a newline (`\n`):

### 2.1 Initialization Request & Response

#### Request
```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": {
      "name": "antigravity-cli",
      "version": "2.0.0"
    }
  }
}
```

#### Response
```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "result": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {
      "tools": {}
    },
    "serverInfo": {
      "name": "christina",
      "version": "1.0.0"
    }
  }
}
```

---

## 3. The 4 Canonical FastMCP Tools

Christina consolidates all cognitive capabilities into 4 unified, orthogonal MCP tools:

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                             CANONICAL MCP TAXONOMY                            |
|                                                                               |
|   1. cpg_query         -> Dynamic AST & Code Property Graph Radar             |
|   2. rlm_execute       -> Sandboxed RLM Runtime & Cognitive Governor          |
|   3. memory_evolve     -> Durable Semantic Memory & Global Distillery         |
|   4. swarm_blackboard  -> Swarm OCC Concurrency & Linda Tuple Space           |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

---

### 3.1 `cpg_query`

Topological AST radar and Code Property Graph engine: def-use chains, CFG traversal, polyglot virtual interfaces, blast radius analysis, God nodes, cycle detection, and execution waves.

#### JSON Schema
```json
{
  "name": "cpg_query",
  "description": "CPG & AST radar: def-use chains, CFG, virtual interfaces, blast radius.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "symbol": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Target symbol name or qualified ID (e.g. 'AuthService', 'module.py::func')."
      },
      "mode": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "blast_radius",
          "def_use",
          "cfg",
          "vinterfaces",
          "god_nodes",
          "cycles",
          "waves",
          "info"
        ],
        "default": "blast_radius",
        "description": "Analysis query mode."
      },
      "depth": {
        "type": "integer",
        "default": 3,
        "description": "Maximum traversal depth for recursive CTE blast radius."
      },
      "code": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Optional inline source code snippet to parse and extract Braun SSA/def-use chains dynamically."
      },
      "file_path": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Optional virtual file path for snippet parsing."
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### Query Modes:
| Mode | Description | Key Output Fields |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `blast_radius` | Transitive caller and callee closure via SQL recursive CTE | `target_symbol`, `callers`, `callees`, `affected_files`, `total_impact_count`, `risk_score` |
| `def_use` | Variable definition-to-use chains and Braun SSA $\phi$-nodes | `def_use_chains` |
| `cfg` | Control flow graph edges (basic block branches and loops) | `cfg_edges` |
| `vinterfaces` | Polyglot virtual interfaces (PyO3, gRPC Proto, OpenAPI, Ctypes) | `virtual_interfaces` |
| `god_nodes` | High-centrality architectural bottlenecks ranked by composite degree | `god_nodes` |
| `cycles` | Circular dependency cycles detected via iterative Tarjan SCC | `cycles` |
| `waves` | Non-colliding parallel execution waves via Kahn topological sort | `waves` |
| `info` | Detailed symbol metadata, location, and LOC metrics | `symbol`, `node` |

#### Example Invocation: Blast Radius
```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 10,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "cpg_query",
    "arguments": {
      "symbol": "AuthService",
      "mode": "blast_radius",
      "depth": 3
    }
  }
}
```

#### Example Result:
```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 10,
  "result": {
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\n  \"target_symbol\": \"services.auth::AuthService\",\n  \"callers\": [\n    \"routes.login::handle_login\",\n    \"middleware.jwt::verify_session\"\n  ],\n  \"callees\": [\n    \"database.client::get_db_session\",\n    \"utils.crypto::verify_argon2\"\n  ],\n  \"affected_files\": [\n    \"database/client.py\",\n    \"middleware/jwt.py\",\n    \"routes/login.py\",\n    \"services/auth.py\",\n    \"utils/crypto.py\"\n  ],\n  \"total_impact_count\": 4,\n  \"risk_score\": 0.333\n}"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

